NAME
	scene-fixture (service) - mount a scenefs at its mount point and drive it with scenedemo, a synthetic field survey

INTERFACE
	service (MatrixService)

READS
	nothing

WRITES
	<mount>/log	scene records (docs/scene-design.md §3.2): six rovers
			mowing lanes, a relay, a base and its radio range,
			one tick per second of scene time, every 200 ms

DESCRIPTION
	init() mounts a scenefs at the mount point unless one is already
	there, so a composition works from the picker with nothing else
	running.  Rovers out of radio reach are reported at their last
	known position with stale= set, so viewers draw them dimmed.
	The mount is the grant: service scene-fixture /mnt/scene.

SEE ALSO
	wm/scene, scenefs(4), scenedemo(1)
